WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.213
-Welcome, everybody.

00:00:01.213 --> 00:00:03.769
Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.769 --> 00:00:05.071
Thank you for being here.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:07.406
Thank you for watching.

00:00:07.406 --> 00:00:10.043
Well, guys, earlier tonight,
President Biden delivered

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:12.078
his first joint address
to Congress

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:15.281
on the eve of his
100th day in office.

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:17.683
Last time someone in their 70s
got that much applause,

00:00:17.683 --> 00:00:19.385
they were doing "Da Butt."

00:00:19.385 --> 00:00:20.786
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.786 --> 00:00:24.991
-Yeah!
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:27.260
-Come on.
-That's right.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.195
The Capitol
took center stage tonight,

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.996
and I got to be honest,
it was nice to see someone

00:00:30.996 --> 00:00:34.434
behind the podium who wasn't
wearing deer antlers and a pelt.

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:35.735
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:38.337
Yeah, it was a fun night
for Democrats.

00:00:38.337 --> 00:00:40.907
On the other hand, Republicans
didn't seem too thrilled.

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:42.608
They looked like
they just heard their best hope

00:00:42.608 --> 00:00:44.577
in 2024 is Randy Quaid.

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:46.946
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:50.216
Of course, Vice President
Kamala Harris sat behind Biden.

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:51.917
She had a spray bottle
just in case he started

00:00:51.917 --> 00:00:53.019
drifting off topic.

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:56.422
It's like -- "Joe, Joe, Joe!

00:00:56.422 --> 00:00:59.158
No, Joe! No, stop!"
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:59.158 --> 00:01:00.359
"Let's get on with it.
Come on.

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:02.361
Back -- Focus."

00:01:02.361 --> 00:01:04.831
Due to COVID, this was not
a typical joint address.

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:07.467
For instance, all the lawmakers
were seated far apart

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:09.869
for social distancing,
which was too bad

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:12.372
'cause they couldn't do the
usual Congressional kiss cam.

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:15.341
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:17.710
On CBS,
the address aired right after

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:20.012
"The Price is Right at Night,"

00:01:20.012 --> 00:01:21.847
which was why Biden
was introduced with,

00:01:21.847 --> 00:01:24.417
"Joe Biden, come on down!"

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:28.121
♪♪

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:30.356
[ Applause ]

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:33.025
Yeah, I think there might
have been a cross promotion,

00:01:33.025 --> 00:01:35.661
because after unveiling
his American Families Plan,

00:01:35.661 --> 00:01:40.033
Biden was like, "And the actual
retail price, $1.8 trillion!"

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:42.168
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:43.502
That's right,
during his address,

00:01:43.502 --> 00:01:48.006
Biden unveiled his $1.8 trillion
American Families Plan.

00:01:48.006 --> 00:01:50.843
At first, people thought he said
"American Family Plan,"

00:01:50.843 --> 00:01:52.879
like we're all going to hop on
the same Verizon account.

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:56.682
It's like, "It's a genius idea!
We all share the same bill!

00:01:56.682 --> 00:01:58.484
300 million people."

00:01:58.484 --> 00:02:02.889
A big part of the plan includes
free universal preschool.

00:02:02.889 --> 00:02:04.523
-Whoo!
-Yeah, I think that's --

00:02:04.523 --> 00:02:08.060
[ Cheers and applause ]
I think that's pretty good.

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:10.296
Pretty good, considering sending
your kid to preschool now

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:11.864
is just handing them an iPad.

00:02:11.864 --> 00:02:13.166
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:14.367
Now this is big.
Earlier today,

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:16.736
federal Investigators
raided Rudy Giuliani's

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:19.005
Manhattan apartment and office

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:22.007
because of his dealings
in Ukraine.

00:02:22.007 --> 00:02:23.943
When the agents walked in,
Rudy got so nervous,

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:25.144
he started sweating hair dye

00:02:25.144 --> 00:02:26.813
and tucking all the evidence
down his pants.

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:27.947
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:31.584
[ As Borat ] "My wife."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:33.152
[ Normal voice] Rudy was like,
"Why, I have nothing to hide

00:02:33.152 --> 00:02:35.221
except for everything
past this door."

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:36.556
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:38.324
Yeah, Rudy panicked
and called his lawyer,

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:39.859
then when his own phone
started ringing,

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:41.561
he panicked even more.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:44.664
"No!"

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:47.433
Well, guys, a lot of people have
road trips planned this summer,

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:49.969
but I just saw that gas stations
all over the country

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:53.373
could run out of gas
in the coming months.

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:55.508
It's gonna be a tough summer,
especially because gasoline

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:57.944
is the main ingredient
in White Claw Surge.

00:02:57.944 --> 00:02:59.946
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:02.915
There's my man.
One area.

00:03:02.915 --> 00:03:04.950
-Wow!
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:07.052
Now you know.
-That's it, yeah.

00:03:07.052 --> 00:03:08.721
The people waiting online
for "The Tonight Show,"

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:10.122
everybody gets
a White Claw Surge.

00:03:10.122 --> 00:03:12.358
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:03:12.358 --> 00:03:15.695
That is a rowdy area.
That -- [ Laughs ]

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:17.629
My God.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:17.629 --> 00:03:20.032
-Meanwhile, toymaker Hasbro
just said that it would

00:03:20.032 --> 00:03:22.368
raise the prices
of its games and toys

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:25.104
as the cost
of raw materials increases.

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:27.173
Yeah, now they're
just selling boxes that say,

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:29.909
"Toy not included."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:32.311
Some more business news --
Chipotle is giving away

00:03:32.311 --> 00:03:36.249
250,000 burritos to nurses
and healthcare workers

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:38.618
in honor of National Nurses Day.

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:42.454
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:42.454 --> 00:03:44.690
Not only is that great news
for healthcare workers,

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:47.193
but I think we also just solved
the gas shortage.

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:50.496
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:51.730
-Wow.

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:56.301
I saw that Rotten Tomatoes
now ranks "Paddington 2"

00:03:56.301 --> 00:04:00.840
ahead of "Citizen Kane" as the
best reviewed film of all time.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.675
White Claw people love
"Paddington 2."

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:04.977
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:04:04.977 --> 00:04:07.112
Yeah, "Paddington 2."
It's a great movie,

00:04:07.112 --> 00:04:09.181
but it's pretty surprising
that the number-one slot

00:04:09.181 --> 00:04:11.650
isn't one of Paddington's
more dramatic movies.

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:14.554
I mean, just this year,
he was in "NoPantsLand."

00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:15.755
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.755 --> 00:04:18.591
Year before that,
he was in "Bearasite."

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:20.359
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.359 --> 00:04:23.795
-[ Thinking ] That's it, Tariq.
Just keep fake laughing.

00:04:23.795 --> 00:04:26.266
It is almost the weekend.

00:04:26.266 --> 00:04:29.402
-There's also
"Mar Me By Your Lade."

00:04:29.402 --> 00:04:31.003
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.003 --> 00:04:34.374
-[ Thinking ] Man, I was
at the Oscars on Sunday.

00:04:34.374 --> 00:04:36.476
I should have stayed my ass
in L.A.

00:04:36.476 --> 00:04:39.144
-And, of course,
who could forget classics like

00:04:39.144 --> 00:04:41.347
"The Coatbook."

00:04:41.347 --> 00:04:44.951
-Holy [bleep]
This is great!

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:48.454
Fallon, you've changed
the late-night game once again.

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:50.289
[ Laughing ]

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:52.825
-And, of course, "Bravehat."

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:56.195
[ Laughter ]
[ Laughing ] Oh, my God.

00:04:56.195 --> 00:04:59.498
[ Laughing ]
-Glad you guys enjoyed that.

00:04:59.498 --> 00:05:01.200
-Oh, my God.
-That bit.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.435
-[ Laughing ]
"Bravehat"!

00:05:03.435 --> 00:05:05.604
-Some, uh...
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.604 --> 00:05:07.039
Some more entertainment news.

00:05:07.039 --> 00:05:09.641
After the success
of "Godzilla vs. Kong,"

00:05:09.641 --> 00:05:11.444
they're already thinking about
the next movie,

00:05:11.444 --> 00:05:14.013
which could be called
"Son of Kong."

00:05:14.013 --> 00:05:15.548
-Ooh.
-Yep.

00:05:15.548 --> 00:05:17.983
It starts with King Kong going,
"You're my son?

00:05:17.983 --> 00:05:20.253
Damn, that clinic said that
you'd never be able to find me."

00:05:20.253 --> 00:05:22.889
[ Laughter ]

00:05:22.889 --> 00:05:25.090
Yeah, it is about a giant ape
who doesn't want to go into

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:27.793
his family's
lizard-punching business.

00:05:27.793 --> 00:05:29.595
"I'm different than you, Dad!"

00:05:29.595 --> 00:05:32.632
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.632 --> 00:05:34.567
And this is fun --
they're also planning a movie

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:36.068
that takes place before
"Son of Kong,"

00:05:36.068 --> 00:05:37.603
called "How I Met Your Monkey."

00:05:37.603 --> 00:05:40.172
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.172 --> 00:05:42.975
-[ Laughing loudly ]

00:05:42.975 --> 00:05:45.011
[ Laughter ]

00:05:45.011 --> 00:05:47.980
-Well, guys --
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:50.850
Well, guys, it's now been over
a year since we all got on Zoom,

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:52.918
and yet some people are still
getting the hang of it,

00:05:52.918 --> 00:05:54.320
even people on the news.

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:56.022
So you know what that means.
It's time for another

00:05:56.022 --> 00:05:58.357
installment of "Greatest Moments
in Zoom History."

00:05:58.357 --> 00:05:59.358
Enjoy.

00:05:59.358 --> 00:06:02.828
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:02.828 --> 00:06:06.699
-And it went viral because --

00:06:06.699 --> 00:06:10.035
-As soon as the Congresswoman
said "viral," she froze.

00:06:10.035 --> 00:06:11.803
-I now call upon
the prime minister

00:06:11.803 --> 00:06:14.073
of the Republic of India,
his excellency Narendra Modi.

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:17.409
-Your excellency,
President Biden.

00:06:17.409 --> 00:06:19.245
[ Phone dialing ]

00:06:19.245 --> 00:06:22.748
Colleagues.
My fellow citizens.

00:06:22.748 --> 00:06:23.816
[ Phone dialing ]

00:06:23.816 --> 00:06:24.851
-Well, I guess we could,
you know,

00:06:24.851 --> 00:06:28.721
good old college try, I suppose.

00:06:28.721 --> 00:06:30.756
-[ No audio ]

00:06:30.756 --> 00:06:35.128
[ Laughter ]

00:06:35.128 --> 00:06:36.362
-If you're near the White House,

00:06:36.362 --> 00:06:40.165
what's the mood like
among the crowd there?

00:06:40.165 --> 00:06:43.602
[ Repetitive static ]

00:06:43.602 --> 00:06:45.738
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:45.738 --> 00:06:48.007
-[ Laughing ]

00:06:48.007 --> 00:06:52.711
[ Loud tapping ]

00:06:52.711 --> 00:06:55.548
At this point, we've all heard
some crazy conspiracy theories

00:06:55.548 --> 00:06:58.383
about the vaccine,
but check out how a doctor

00:06:58.383 --> 00:07:00.319
reacted yesterday
when a Republican lawmaker

00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:02.822
was pressing him
on one of the theories.

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:18.070
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:26.178 --> 00:07:31.117
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:31.117 --> 00:07:33.519
-Come on.

00:07:33.519 --> 00:07:35.721
-The lawmaker was then like,
"Okay. So maybe I won't ask

00:07:35.721 --> 00:07:36.923
my next question
about the vaccine

00:07:36.923 --> 00:07:39.524
turning us into wolf people."
[ Laughter ]

00:07:39.524 --> 00:07:41.393
He could have saved himself
some embarrassment

00:07:41.393 --> 00:07:42.495
if he had just
looked up the answer

00:07:42.495 --> 00:07:44.897
on the tracking device
in his pocket.

00:07:44.897 --> 00:07:47.433
[ Laughter ]

00:07:47.433 --> 00:07:49.534
The phone is tracking you,
buddy!

00:07:49.534 --> 00:07:51.937
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:51.937 --> 00:07:53.438
"Fitbit says I did 10,000 --"

00:07:53.438 --> 00:07:57.109
Yeah, it knows exactly
where you stepped.

00:07:57.109 --> 00:07:59.378
I heard about a mix-up
at a vaccination site

00:07:59.378 --> 00:08:02.415
that put one California woman
in a peculiar situation,

00:08:02.415 --> 00:08:04.850
but she doesn't seem to be
too worried about it.

00:08:04.850 --> 00:08:06.952
Listen to this.
-89 years of life,

00:08:06.952 --> 00:08:10.155
Joanne Lawton's learned one
very important lesson.

00:08:10.155 --> 00:08:13.359
-What good would it do
to be afraid of anything?

00:08:13.359 --> 00:08:16.462
-Even after
she got her COVID-19 vaccine,

00:08:16.462 --> 00:08:20.299
the first dose from Pfizer
and the second from Moderna.

00:08:20.299 --> 00:08:25.204
-How do you feel
that you have two separate --

00:08:25.204 --> 00:08:28.641
-I feel no different,
and I don't give a darn.

00:08:28.641 --> 00:08:30.710
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:30.710 --> 00:08:34.246
-That's what I'm talking about.
[ Laughs ]

00:08:34.246 --> 00:08:36.115
-Yeah.
-That's what I am talking about.

00:08:36.115 --> 00:08:37.783
That Republican lawmaker
was like, "Geez.

00:08:37.783 --> 00:08:39.819
Now you have two
tracking devices in you!"

00:08:39.819 --> 00:08:42.788
[ Laughter ]

00:08:42.788 --> 00:08:45.357
And finally, a man in Oklahoma
got into a bit of an accident

00:08:45.357 --> 00:08:47.726
while trying to park.
Watch this.

00:08:47.726 --> 00:08:50.329
-A car caught on camera
after smashing into

00:08:50.329 --> 00:08:52.064
an Oklahoma middle school.

00:08:52.064 --> 00:08:54.133
Police posting this picture
of the damage and the debris

00:08:54.133 --> 00:08:55.334
to social media.

00:08:55.334 --> 00:08:57.603
They say a man was trying
to park his Mercedes.

00:08:57.603 --> 00:08:59.872
Well, he accidentally
put the S.U.V. into drive

00:08:59.872 --> 00:09:02.707
instead of reverse and slammed
right through the school's wall.

00:09:02.707 --> 00:09:04.510
Luckily, no one was hurt.

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:06.979
[ Laughter ]

00:09:06.979 --> 00:09:08.847
-He tried to play it off
by hopping out of the car

00:09:08.847 --> 00:09:09.849
like the Kool-Aid Man.

00:09:09.849 --> 00:09:11.684
"Oh, yeah!"

